+## Realtime inference without tool calls

threads.body:
Input transcription can arrive in multiple chunks before model output; it does not establish that generation has started. [Gemini gives no ordering guarantee](https://ai.google.dev/api/live#BidiGenerateContentServerContent), and [ADK accumulates the chunks](https://github.com/google/adk-python/blob/main/src/google/adk/models/gemini_llm_connection.py). Could we accumulate input transcription without opening the span, then start on model output or the existing tool-call branch? The mock should send multiple input-transcription chunks before output to demonstrate this.

Add `input_transcript_deltas = []` before the receive loop, then:

```suggestion
        if server_content is not None:
            if server_content.input_transcription and server_content.input_transcription.text:
                input_transcript_deltas.append(server_content.input_transcription.text)
                input_messages = _user_transcription_message("".join(input_transcript_deltas))
                if span is not None:
                    span.set_attribute("gen_ai.input.messages", input_messages)
            if span is None and (
                server_content.model_turn
                or (server_content.output_transcription and server_content.output_transcription.text)
            ):
                span = _reference_tracer.start_span(
                    f"realtime_inference {request_model}", kind=SpanKind.CLIENT, attributes=attributes
                )
                span.set_attribute("gen_ai.input.messages", input_messages)
```
